  "_about": "Codes pulled from the Census International Trade API (KAN-282). Only codes that stand for one ingredient: tier A = mostly a supplement / nutrient ingredient, A2 = one ingredient but dominated by food / feed / industry use. Mixed (basket) codes are not pulled. Import codes: HTS 2026 lines checked in the KAN-282 pilot (each returned 12 months of data). Export codes: Schedule B 2026 concordance (census.gov sbsdf.zip econcord.txt), kept only when the line is the same single ingredient; vitamin D, biotin, glucosamine, glycine, mint leaves, inositol (with sterols) and gelatin (with photographic gelatin) have no such export line. 0909.61 (anise / badian / caraway / fennel) was dropped as a basket. 'ingredient' is a label for people; the mapping to Supply Smart substances is made on the Supply Smart side.",
